From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:51:32 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: xrx500-phy-fw: sleep through the firmware boot delay

After the per-PHY reset loop, the probe waits 100 ms for the GPHY
firmware to come up. It waited with mdelay(), which busy-spins a CPU for
the whole 100 ms. Probe context can sleep, so it should: msleep() gives
the time back to whatever else wants to run during boot. Nothing here
holds a lock or runs with interrupts off.

AVM's 08.25 GPL release makes the same change (msleep(100) in
drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c of Linux 4.9.337,
against mdelay(100) at :141 of Linux 4.9.198).

That one line is the whole of what is taken from AVM's rewrite of this
file. The rest of 08.25's version is a multi-SoC restructuring whose
fixes this port already made independently, mostly better: a per-PHY
devm_reset_control_get() instead of AVM's single file-scope reset
pointer that each iteration clobbers -- which this file's header comment
has called out as a latent AVM bug since it was written -- an ioremap
driven by the DT reg property, a managed DMA allocation, and silicon-id
validation before anything touches reset control. AVM's
devm_reset_control_get_optional() is specifically not adopted: both our
device trees declare every PHY, so a missing reset line is a broken DT
rather than a configuration, and the mandatory get with its named error
message says which line is missing.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c
index dbf7ad6680ce..1d2c0861f09f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/xrx500_phy_fw.c
@@ -493,7 +493,8 @@ static int xway_phy_fw_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	mdelay(100);
+	/* Let the GPHY firmware boot. Probe context sleeps; no need to spin. */
+	msleep(100);
 
 	pr_info("xrx500-phy-fw: loaded %s size=%zu sha256-prefix=%02x%02x%02x%02x%02x%02x%02x%02x\n",
 		fw_name, fw_size,
